     "polygon",
     "regular",
     "base and height"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of its three sides. 30 plus 40 plus 50 is 120 m.\nFor a regular polygon all sides are equal, so perimeter is number of sides times side length. A regular hexagon with side 5 cm has perimeter 30 cm.\nThe area of a triangle is half of base times height. A triangle with base 6 cm and height 4 cm has area 12 square cm."
    }
